    "created_at": "2026-04-09T10:42:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-09T10:42:13Z",
    "body": "Fwiw I don't think we should enforce this at the parser level, if we in future come up with ways to fix \"nested interactives\" then we'd have to make yet another parser change. In fact a world where aria-actions exists might mean that this is a legitimate pattern (I'm not an expert I could be completely misunderstanding that).\n\nWe should already be handling this in the content model, but we discussed this during the long road of incubating and I think there was largely consensus to *not* block authors from doing this sort of thing.",
